usage
=====

boot is handled by /etc/rc.boot and shutdown by /etc/rc.shutdown, both
run by busybox init via /etc/inittab. runit (runsvdir /var/service)
starts services after boot.

local customization (these files are kept across upgrades, don't edit
rc.boot/rc.shutdown directly):

  /etc/rc.boot.local       commands run at the end of boot
  /etc/rc.shutdown.local   commands run at shutdown
  /etc/rc.modules          kernel modules to load at boot, one per line
  /etc/sysctl.conf         applied with 'sysctl -p' at boot if present

kernel command line options:

  fastboot     skip filesystem check
  forcefsck    force filesystem check

if /var/service/mdevd exists, rc.boot leaves device setup to mdevd
instead of busybox mdev.
